data: {"type": "assistant_msg", "ts": "2026-08-06T12:10:34.874582+00:00", "content": "Based on the telemetry gathered, here is the **network-wide incident digest for the last 24 hours**:\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udd34 **Major Incident: Network-Wide BGP Adjacency Flap**  \n**Time:** 2026-08-05 17:24:42 \u2013 17:24:43 UTC (single ~1-second burst)  \n**Scope:** **All 24 branch CE routers + 12 PE routers + 6 hub CE routers + 4 DC CE routers** (\u2248100 BGP sessions across VRFs `vrf_CORP` and `vrf_VOICE`)  \n**Symptom:** Simultaneous `%ADJCHANGE: neighbor \u2026 Down Interface down` on every CE\u2194PE and hub\u2194PE BGP peering.  \n**Evidence:** 64 log lines captured in the window, e.g.:\n- `ce_branch1` \u2194 `pe1` (10.1.0.1) VRF `vrf_CORP` [events:0]\n- `ce_branch11` \u2194 `pe11` (10.1.0.41) VRF `vrf_CORP` [events:1]\n- `ce_branch12` \u2194 `pe12` (10.1.0.45) VRF `vrf_CORP` [events:2]\n- `ce_branch13` \u2194 `pe1` (10.1.0.49) VRF `vrf_CORP` [events:3]\n- `ce_branch16` \u2194 `pe4` (10.1.0.61) VRF `vrf_CORP` [events:4]\n- \u2026and 58 more covering every branch/hub/DC CE and every PE [events:5]\u2013[events:63]\n- Both VRFs (`vrf_CORP` and `vrf_VOICE`) flipped together on dual-VRF branches (e.g., `ce_branch11` VRF `vrf_VOICE` [events:31], `ce_branch14` VRF `vrf_VOICE` [events:33], `ce_branch7` VRF `vrf_VOICE` [events:44], etc.).\n\n**Root-cause indicator:** \u201cInterface down\u201d on the **PE-CE link** (not BGP hold-timer expiry), suggesting a **Layer-1/2 underlay flap** (transport circuit, cross-connect, or MPLS LSP) that took all CE\u2194PE interfaces down at once.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udfe2 **Current Recovery Status (as of latest metrics poll \u2248 1786017990 / 2026-08-05 19:26:30 UTC)**\n\n| Device / Role | BGP Peers Established | Expected | Prefix Counts (CORP/VOICE/GUEST) | Notes |\n|---------------|----------------------|----------|----------------------------------|-------|\n| **pe1** (core PE) | **11** [metrics:2] | 11 | 67 / 67 / 19 [metrics:3]\u2013[metrics:5] | **Fully recovered** |\n| **pe2** (core PE) | **11** [metrics:2] | 11 | 67 / 67 / 19 [metrics:3]\u2013[metrics:5] | **Fully recovered** |\n| **pe7** (edge PE) | **2** [metrics:2] | ~11 | 67 / 67 / 19 [metrics:3]\u2013[metrics:5] | **Partially recovered** \u2013 only 2 peers up |\n| **pe8** (edge PE) | **2** [metrics:2] | ~11 | 67 / 67 / 19 [metrics:3]\u2013[metrics:5] | **Partially recovered** \u2013 only 2 peers up |\n| **pe11** (edge PE) | **2** [topo:pe11] | ~11 | 67 / 67 / 19 [topo:pe11] | **Partially recovered** |\n| **pe12** (edge PE) | **2** [topo:pe12] | ~11 | 67 / 67 / 19 [topo:pe12] | **Partially recovered** |\n| **ce_branch1** (sample branch) | N/A (no BGP metric exported) | \u2014 | \u2014 | Hardware & interfaces healthy [metrics:0]\u2013[metrics:3]; SD-WAN tunnel **up** (latency 20.7 ms, loss 0.13 %) [topo:ce_branch1] |\n| **ce_branch12/24** (pe12 downstreams) | \u2014 | \u2014 | \u2014 | Interfaces **OperStatus=1** [topo:ce_branch12], [topo:ce_branch24]; SD-WAN tunnels **up** (latency 54\u201390 ms) [topo:ce_branch12], [topo:ce_branch24] |\n\n**Interpretation:** Core PEs (pe1, pe2) have fully re-established all 11 BGP peers. Edge PEs (pe7, pe8, pe11, pe12) are stuck at only 2 peers each \u2014 their downstream branches/hubs are **not yet re-peered** over the CORP/VOICE VRFs despite the underlay interfaces showing `ifOperStatus=1`.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udd0e **Blast-Radius / Downstream Impact** (from `walk_topology_graph`)\n- **pe1** downstreams: `ce_branch1`, `ce_branch13`, `ce_hub1`, `p3`, `p4` \u2014 all **interface-up, hardware healthy** [topo:pe1].\n- **pe12** downstreams: `ce_branch12`, `ce_branch24`, `p23`, `p24` \u2014 all **interface-up**, but `ce_branch24` shows **elevated SD-WAN jitter (34 ms) & latency (91 ms)** [topo:ce_branch24] \u2014 possible congestion on the recovered path.\n- Core P-routers (`p1`\u2013`p4`, `p21`\u2013`p24`) show **zero discards/errors, OSPF/MPLS stable** [topo:pe1], [topo:pe12].\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udccb **Suggested Next Actions (aligned with runbook patterns)**\n1. **Verify underlay LSP/transport health** on the four edge PEs (pe7, pe8, pe11, pe12) \u2014 check MPLS LDP/LSP state, optical RX power, cross-connects.  \n2. **Force BGP session reset** on the stuck edge PEs for the missing peers (`clear bgp ipv4 vrf CORP * soft in/out` then hard if needed).  \n3. **Correlate with carrier/transport NOC** \u2014 the simultaneous \u201cInterface down\u201d across all PE-CE links at 17:24:42 points to a **common transport event** (fiber cut, DWDM card reboot, MPLS core flap).  \n4. **Monitor `ce_branch24` SD-WAN path** \u2014 latency/jitter spike may indicate sub-optimal failover path after recovery.  \n5. **Open post-incident review** \u2014 capture carrier RCA, update runbook \u201cBGP Mass Flap / Underlay Failure\u201d with this timeline.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udccc **Key Evidence Citations**\n- BGP mass flap logs: [events:0]\u2013[events:63]  \n- Current BGP peer counts & prefix tables: [metrics:0]\u2013[metrics:5] (pe1), [metrics:0]\u2013[metrics:5] (pe2), [metrics:0]\u2013[metrics:5] (pe7), [metrics:0]\u2013[metrics:5] (pe8)  \n- Topology blast-radius & live status: [topo:pe1], [topo:pe12], [topo:ce_branch1], [topo:ce_branch12], [topo:ce_branch24]  \n\n---\n\n**Bottom line:** A **single-second, network-wide Layer-1/2 event** dropped every CE\u2194PE interface at 17:24:42 UTC. Core has self-healed; **four edge PEs remain partially isolated** \u2014 focus troubleshooting there first."}

